```catala
declaration many_vars content (list of anything of type a,
                               list of anything of type b,
                               list of anything of type c,
                               list of anything of type d,
                               list of anything of type c,
                               list of anything of type b,
                               list of anything of type e)
  depends on dummy content anything of type b
  equals ([], [], [dummy], [], [], [], [])
```

The message is good, but only detected in dcalc (and therefore marked "internal"
and not raised by `catala typecheck`)

```catala-test-cli
$ catala lcalc
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  This function has type
│  <b> →
│    (list of <a>,
│     list of <b>,
│     list of <b>,
│     list of <d>,
│     list of <b>,
│     list of <b>,
│     list of <e>)
│  which requires that <c> = <b>, while they are both specified as
│  "anything".
│
├─➤ tests/typing/bad/linked_vars.catala_en:3.57-3.58:
│   │
│ 3 │                                list of anything of type b,
│   │                                                         ‾
└─
#return code 123#
```
